1
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,920
<i>- Get something to tie her up!
- Let me go!</i>

2
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:04,520
<i>This time, I'll bind your souls.</i>

3
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:07,913
<i>You'll never be reborn,
not in a billion lifetimes!</i>

4
00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:14,324
<i>She just fainted,
and you took her to the hospital.</i>

5
00:01:14,324 --> 00:01:15,890
<i>Yo's test results are in.</i>

6
00:01:15,890 --> 00:01:18,494
<i>The drug she was given
damaged her nervous system.</i>

7
00:01:18,494 --> 00:01:20,425
<i>I told you to use just a little!</i>

8
00:01:20,425 --> 00:01:23,706
<i>If anything happens to Yo,
I'll go to the police!</i>

9
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:28,906
<i>Yo...</i>

10
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:33,520
Please forgive me, Yo.

11
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:36,320
I promise I'll never do it again.

12
00:01:36,320 --> 00:01:38,768
You said you loved me so much.

13
00:01:38,768 --> 00:01:40,159
Then prove it.

14
00:01:40,159 --> 00:01:43,733
Those two women were in on it with you.

15
00:01:43,733 --> 00:01:46,410
Which one will you deal with first?

16
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:51,706
Can't choose?

17
00:01:53,760 --> 00:01:55,120
Then...

18
00:01:56,568 --> 00:01:58,455
I choose you...

19
00:01:58,455 --> 00:02:01,506
My dear husband.

20
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:08,106
Yo!

21
00:02:12,638 --> 00:02:13,906
Yo!

22
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:18,813
Yo...

23
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:26,513
Keep your voice down.

24
00:02:27,412 --> 00:02:30,006
Or hell might find you.

25
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:45,013
Yo...

26
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:49,400
Pam!

27
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:50,820
In the mirror!

28
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:54,620
It's strangling Nat through the mirror!

29
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:10,013
Let him go, you crazy ghost!

30
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:16,720
Nat!

31
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:18,920
Nat!

32
00:03:18,920 --> 00:03:20,506
Are you okay?

33
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:24,713
We should get Nat out of here.

34
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:40,638
Wherever you run, you can't escape us!

35
00:03:40,638 --> 00:03:43,500
Because I'll do to you what you did to us!

36
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:15,009
Now... you'll taste the same suffering we did!

37
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:59,403
You think you can escape, Sroi?

38
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:25,013
Will you cut it yourself,
or should I do it for you?

39
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:33,513
Where am I?

40
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:39,120
Help!

41
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:43,419
Somebody help me!

42
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:55,513
Pete! Help me!

43
00:06:57,760 --> 00:06:59,213
Pete!

44
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:01,280
Can you hear me?

45
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:04,960
[ICU 3 - Yotaka Thanahirankit]
[Dr. Atchariya Pengyasa]

46
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:30,000
Yes, Uncle?

47
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:33,293
I tried to help Yo, but I couldn't.

48
00:07:33,293 --> 00:07:35,566
Please hurry and help her.

49
00:07:35,566 --> 00:07:38,013
But Yo's in the hospital.

50
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:40,630
<i>That's just her body.</i>

51
00:07:40,630 --> 00:07:43,013
<i>Her spirit is still trapped there.</i>

52
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:46,290
What should I do?

53
00:07:46,290 --> 00:07:48,539
Focus your mind.

54
00:07:48,539 --> 00:07:50,513
Think only of Yo.

55
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,313
Yes, Uncle.

56
00:08:29,848 --> 00:08:31,113
Yo!

57
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:36,513
Pete!

58
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:39,606
Yo.

59
00:08:44,320 --> 00:08:45,910
How did this happen?

60
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:52,306
I think I'm trapped here.

61
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:56,206
You two must stay here!

62
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:01,800
No... Yo and I won't stay here.

63
00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:04,840
Neither of us owes you any karmic debt.

64
00:09:04,840 --> 00:09:07,013
Why are you keeping us here?

65
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:15,413
Yo... focus. Come back with me.

66
00:09:18,484 --> 00:09:20,813
You'll never escape!

67
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,313
Yo!

68
00:09:31,010 --> 00:09:32,306
Yo!

69
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:34,480
Yo!

70
00:09:36,381 --> 00:09:37,713
Yo!

71
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:42,800
Go back!

72
00:09:43,810 --> 00:09:44,920
No!

73
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:52,600
I'm going to find Yo.

74
00:09:53,640 --> 00:09:55,400
I love her.

75
00:09:56,400 --> 00:10:00,313
Just as Pan loved Sali.

76
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,206
Please let me take Yo back.

77
00:10:13,617 --> 00:10:15,200
Let Yo and me go.

78
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:16,613
You know very well...

79
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:21,020
Yo never meant you any harm.

80
00:10:24,400 --> 00:10:26,313
Please let Yo go.

81
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,413
I'll let her go.

82
00:10:36,907 --> 00:10:39,260
But she might not go back with you.

83
00:10:39,260 --> 00:10:40,813
Because she loves Lert.

84
00:10:48,880 --> 00:10:50,100
Kadkao!

85
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:56,353
Kadkao... I love you, Kadkao.

86
00:10:56,353 --> 00:10:58,800
Don't leave me like this, Kadkao.

87
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:02,106
I'll bring you back to life, Kadkao.

88
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:14,461
Help me!

89
00:11:14,461 --> 00:11:16,000
Help me!

90
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:18,400
Whoever brings Kadkao back to life,

91
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:20,400
I'll give them ten chang!

92
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:31,920
Kadkao...

93
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:34,733
I love you, Kadkao.

94
00:11:34,733 --> 00:11:36,606
You mustn't leave me.

95
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:41,540
I'll take you to a shaman.

96
00:11:41,540 --> 00:11:44,113
I'll find a way to bring you back.

97
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:49,040
Master.

98
00:11:49,040 --> 00:11:51,013
Have you gone mad?

99
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:54,050
Trying to bring the dead back to life?

100
00:11:54,050 --> 00:11:55,643
I'm not mad.

101
00:11:55,643 --> 00:11:57,460
I love Kadkao.

102
00:11:57,460 --> 00:11:59,206
What about me?

103
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:02,680
Have you forgotten?

104
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:05,606
We got married because
our families arranged it.

105
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:11,106
Did you ever love me at all, Master?

106
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:17,318
Kadkao is the only one in my heart.

107
00:12:21,040 --> 00:12:22,505
Master...

108
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:26,830
I'll take you to a shaman.

109
00:12:26,830 --> 00:12:29,204
I'll find a way to bring you back.

110
00:12:34,200 --> 00:12:35,305
Bulan, don't!

111
00:12:35,305 --> 00:12:36,680
Bulan, don't!

112
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:37,961
Bulan, don't!

113
00:12:37,961 --> 00:12:39,080
Bulan, don't!

114
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:41,800
- Bulan, don't... Don't!
- Let go!

115
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:43,506
- Don't!
- Let go!

116
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:46,213
I said stop it!

117
00:12:48,920 --> 00:12:50,213
Master!

118
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:58,360
Bulan, don't!

119
00:12:58,360 --> 00:12:59,720
Don't!

120
00:13:02,668 --> 00:13:07,600
Bulan, stop! That's enough, Bulan!

121
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:09,607
Stop this madness!

122
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:13,908
Stop this madness!

123
00:13:19,040 --> 00:13:24,554
My lady, please don't!
Please stop! I'm begging you!

124
00:13:24,554 --> 00:13:27,017
Get out of my way, Sroi!

125
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:31,930
I said get out of my way!

126
00:13:31,930 --> 00:13:36,303
No, ma'am! My lady,
please don't hurt Master Lert!

127
00:13:37,320 --> 00:13:38,843
I told you to get out of my way!

128
00:13:38,843 --> 00:13:42,606
Master Lert, run! Run!

129
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:45,563
Go, sir!

130
00:13:45,563 --> 00:13:46,800
Let go of me!

131
00:13:46,800 --> 00:13:49,160
Master... Master!

132
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:51,400
- Let go!
- No! I won't, ma'am!

133
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:52,680
Let go of me!

134
00:13:52,680 --> 00:13:53,920
Let go!

135
00:13:57,307 --> 00:13:59,706
Do you love him more than me?

136
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:04,763
No, ma'am.

137
00:14:04,763 --> 00:14:07,800
I just don't want you to hurt Master Lert.

138
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:10,713
I don't believe you!

139
00:14:31,800 --> 00:14:37,710
In this life, I've loved
and revered you, my lady.

140
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:41,796
But if there's a next life...

141
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:46,006
I'll choose to love myself.

142
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:48,440
And I'll...

143
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:53,810
I'll never let you hurt me again.

144
00:14:55,480 --> 00:14:56,713
Sroi!

145
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:20,013
Somebody, please help Kadkao!

146
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:23,516
Help Kadkao!

147
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:27,606
Somebody, help me!

148
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:31,843
Kadkao...

149
00:15:31,843 --> 00:15:34,480
I love you, Kadkao.

150
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:37,713
Don't leave me, Kadkao.

151
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:05,100
Kadkao...

152
00:16:59,120 --> 00:17:00,606
Master...

153
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:05,406
Do you know, Master...

154
00:17:07,440 --> 00:17:10,013
When you hurt,

155
00:17:12,840 --> 00:17:15,506
I hurt even more than you do.

156
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:20,210
May this be...

157
00:17:22,135 --> 00:17:25,306
the last pain we ever share.

158
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:46,010
Kadkao...

159
00:18:41,880 --> 00:18:43,713
Master...

160
00:18:46,080 --> 00:18:48,606
You killed me...

161
00:18:49,680 --> 00:18:51,200
Master...

162
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:22,896
In the end,
your love has made you turn on each other.

163
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:30,706
How satisfying!

164
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:36,303
And now you'll take our places in death.

165
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:41,305
And your corpses
will feed the vultures and crows.

166
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:48,625
My curse still stands!

167
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:58,893
You'll never be reborn for a hundred lifetimes!

168
00:19:59,480 --> 00:20:01,013
- Bastard Lert!
- Bastard Lert!

169
00:20:41,800 --> 00:20:44,010
I'll lift the curse on all of you.

170
00:20:51,120 --> 00:20:53,100
- Yo!
- Nat!

171
00:20:53,805 --> 00:20:55,120
Let go of my wife, now!

172
00:20:55,120 --> 00:20:57,160
Why should I listen to you?

173
00:20:57,160 --> 00:20:58,840
Yo has nothing to do with this.

174
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:00,906
She's Kadkao!

175
00:21:01,720 --> 00:21:04,091
What did Kadkao ever do to you?

176
00:21:04,091 --> 00:21:06,960
She's Lert's beloved!

177
00:21:06,960 --> 00:21:08,040
Yes...

178
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:10,700
No matter the lifetime,
I'll always love this woman.

179
00:21:12,720 --> 00:21:15,116
Will you trade your life for hers?

180
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:17,620
How?

181
00:21:18,440 --> 00:21:21,080
You die, she lives!

182
00:21:21,080 --> 00:21:23,606
You live, she dies!

183
00:21:26,040 --> 00:21:29,793
Hey! Don't! I give up! I'm willing to die!

184
00:21:29,793 --> 00:21:34,213
Nat... No! If we die, we die together!

185
00:21:39,520 --> 00:21:41,413
But Yo has nothing to do with this.

186
00:21:42,400 --> 00:21:45,020
I'm begging you. Let her go.

187
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:49,909
These two have nothing to do with this.
Let them go.

188
00:21:51,800 --> 00:21:54,813
You... Lift the curse. Now!

189
00:22:02,400 --> 00:22:04,336
<i>This doll...</i>

190
00:22:04,336 --> 00:22:07,440
<i>has been passed down
through generations to my father.</i>

191
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:10,910
<i>It's an ancient family heirloom.</i>

192
00:22:10,910 --> 00:22:13,210
<i>Take good care of it, Nat.</i>

193
00:22:14,360 --> 00:22:15,710
<i>Yes, Dad.</i>

194
00:22:27,360 --> 00:22:29,113
I truly repent.

195
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:31,805
I ask for forgiveness.

196
00:22:31,805 --> 00:22:33,787
I hereby lift the curse.

197
00:22:33,787 --> 00:22:35,903
May the souls of Pan...

198
00:22:36,760 --> 00:22:37,803
Yohd...

199
00:22:39,040 --> 00:22:40,406
and Sali...

200
00:22:41,800 --> 00:22:43,406
find peace in the afterlife.

201
00:23:19,200 --> 00:23:22,120
I've suffered for over a hundred years.

202
00:23:22,120 --> 00:23:26,200
Cursed and branded as sexual deviants.

203
00:23:26,200 --> 00:23:29,400
All I'll give you is endless vengeance!

204
00:23:33,040 --> 00:23:36,080
He's lifted the curse. Let them go.

205
00:23:36,080 --> 00:23:38,040
Just like that?

206
00:23:38,040 --> 00:23:41,200
After we've suffered for over a century?

207
00:23:41,200 --> 00:23:44,886
It's that simple. You can finally be free.

208
00:23:44,886 --> 00:23:46,681
Let go of your hatred.

209
00:23:46,681 --> 00:23:48,510
Forgive and move on.

210
00:23:49,840 --> 00:23:53,015
You must know I only want what's best for you.

211
00:23:53,015 --> 00:23:54,720
You're my family.

212
00:23:54,720 --> 00:23:56,080
No matter what...

213
00:23:56,080 --> 00:23:57,800
I still love you.

214
00:24:00,040 --> 00:24:02,413
I want your souls to find peace.

215
00:24:07,680 --> 00:24:10,313
Even after everything I've done to you?

216
00:24:11,480 --> 00:24:14,600
I understand your anger and resentment.

217
00:24:14,600 --> 00:24:16,306
Go in peace.

218
00:24:17,895 --> 00:24:20,680
Don't carry this vengeance into another life.

219
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:25,713
At least then,
you won't have to suffer anymore.

220
00:24:42,520 --> 00:24:45,806
Hurry! Take Yo back before it's too late!

221
00:24:47,360 --> 00:24:49,800
Nat... You have to get back into your body.

222
00:24:49,800 --> 00:24:51,600
I'm worried about you.

223
00:24:52,480 --> 00:24:54,160
Go back, Yo.

224
00:24:54,160 --> 00:24:56,406
I don't want you to die, no matter what.

225
00:24:57,240 --> 00:25:00,513
Hurry! Take Yo back before it's too late!

226
00:25:13,920 --> 00:25:17,960
[Police Station for the People]

227
00:25:35,760 --> 00:25:36,800
Pete.

228
00:25:37,920 --> 00:25:39,906
The forensic results are in.

229
00:25:40,680 --> 00:25:41,913
What do they say?

230
00:25:42,880 --> 00:25:45,206
Nat, Pam, and Whan

231
00:25:45,206 --> 00:25:47,500
really did conspire to drug Yo.

232
00:25:47,500 --> 00:25:49,213
All three are going to be arrested.

233
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:02,856
- Hello?
- This is the hospital calling.

234
00:26:02,856 --> 00:26:06,194
<i>We have an update on Yotaka's condition.</i>

235
00:26:06,194 --> 00:26:08,200
How is she?

236
00:26:08,200 --> 00:26:11,460
[Intensive Care Unit (ICU)]

237
00:26:11,460 --> 00:26:14,606
I'm so glad you're awake.

238
00:26:19,760 --> 00:26:22,013
There's something else I need to tell you.

239
00:26:26,640 --> 00:26:30,200
Nat, Pam, and Whan...

240
00:26:31,640 --> 00:26:34,000
They're all guilty of drugging you.

241
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:36,016
It nearly killed you.

242
00:26:49,796 --> 00:26:51,416
I'm worried about Nat.

243
00:26:52,640 --> 00:26:54,813
Is there any way you can help him?

244
00:27:06,880 --> 00:27:08,613
<i>Come on, smile! Let's make a video.</i>

245
00:27:09,640 --> 00:27:12,000
<i>Something to remember this by.</i>

246
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:13,446
<i>Do you love me?</i>

247
00:27:13,446 --> 00:27:17,520
<i>I do! Let's make a video like this every year.
What do you think?</i>

248
00:27:17,520 --> 00:27:19,160
<i>- Sounds good.
- Isn't that sweet?</i>

249
00:27:19,160 --> 00:27:20,996
<i>Of course! I'd love that.</i>

250
00:27:21,880 --> 00:27:23,200
<i>I love you, Yo.</i>

251
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:25,200
<i>- I love you too, Nat.
- Yo...</i>

252
00:27:25,200 --> 00:27:27,503
<i>- Hmm?
- Let's have a baby.</i>

253
00:27:27,503 --> 00:27:29,160
<i>- Are you serious?
- I am!</i>

254
00:27:29,160 --> 00:27:31,551
<i>I'd say... two kids would be enough.</i>

255
00:27:31,551 --> 00:27:32,806
<i>What should we name them?</i>

256
00:27:33,960 --> 00:27:35,040
<i>Home.</i>

257
00:27:35,040 --> 00:27:36,240
<i>Home?</i>

258
00:27:36,240 --> 00:27:40,560
<i>Because coming home
should always make us happy, right, Nat?</i>

259
00:27:40,560 --> 00:27:41,941
<i>Okay, okay. What about the younger one?</i>

260
00:27:41,941 --> 00:27:43,480
<i>- House.
- House?</i>

261
00:27:43,480 --> 00:27:46,503
<i>- Home and House? Like that?
- Yes!</i>

262
00:27:48,280 --> 00:27:50,040
<i>I'm ready. Shall we get started?</i>

263
00:27:50,040 --> 00:27:51,906
<i>Right now?</i>

264
00:28:01,960 --> 00:28:05,413
Thank you for everything we've shared, Nat.

265
00:28:11,560 --> 00:28:13,613
But for the rest of my life...

266
00:28:21,200 --> 00:28:25,006
I'll love myself more than I ever loved you.

267
00:29:28,360 --> 00:29:30,113
I'm still alive?

268
00:29:40,400 --> 00:29:41,706
Pam.

269
00:30:00,880 --> 00:30:02,813
You're safe too, right?

270
00:30:07,120 --> 00:30:09,204
I've made up my mind.

271
00:30:09,204 --> 00:30:10,513
I'm going to become a monk.

272
00:30:13,480 --> 00:30:15,316
How can you become a monk?

273
00:30:16,280 --> 00:30:18,060
Don't pretend you don't know.

274
00:30:18,060 --> 00:30:20,220
The police are coming to arrest us!

275
00:30:20,880 --> 00:30:22,840
We have to run, Nat!

276
00:30:22,840 --> 00:30:24,713
You have to get me out of here!

277
00:30:25,360 --> 00:30:27,000
No.

278
00:30:27,000 --> 00:30:30,213
If I have to go to prison, so be it.

279
00:30:31,640 --> 00:30:33,400
But I'm not!

280
00:30:33,400 --> 00:30:34,740
That's up to you.

281
00:30:34,740 --> 00:30:36,306
Where are you going?

282
00:30:37,720 --> 00:30:39,399
I'm going to see Yo.

283
00:30:41,240 --> 00:30:43,240
Have you lost your mind?

284
00:30:43,240 --> 00:30:46,920
After everything you did to Yo,
she'll never come back to you!

285
00:30:48,600 --> 00:30:50,103
I finally realize...

286
00:30:50,880 --> 00:30:55,305
In the past or in this life,
Yo is the only woman I've ever loved.

287
00:30:57,760 --> 00:31:00,220
And I'll do whatever it takes to win her back.

288
00:31:04,840 --> 00:31:05,920
Nat!

289
00:31:15,800 --> 00:31:17,256
Pam!

290
00:31:17,256 --> 00:31:20,006
Bulan was a fool who worshipped love.

291
00:31:20,640 --> 00:31:22,313
But I'm not!

292
00:31:22,880 --> 00:31:25,026
If you don't love me...

293
00:31:25,026 --> 00:31:26,906
If you won't choose me...

294
00:31:27,480 --> 00:31:29,080
Then die!

295
00:31:29,080 --> 00:31:30,420
Die!

296
00:32:12,760 --> 00:32:15,613
Whan... Help me!

297
00:32:29,600 --> 00:32:31,528
Are you out of your mind?

298
00:32:31,528 --> 00:32:33,506
Why would you stab me?

299
00:32:34,280 --> 00:32:36,113
You killed me...

300
00:33:10,297 --> 00:33:11,800
Nat!

301
00:33:11,800 --> 00:33:13,360
Nat!

302
00:33:13,360 --> 00:33:15,920
Nat! Please... Please don't die!

303
00:33:15,920 --> 00:33:18,316
Nat... Nat!

304
00:33:29,120 --> 00:33:30,206
Nat!

305
00:33:37,279 --> 00:33:38,600
Nat!

306
00:35:40,800 --> 00:35:43,210
What the hell am I supposed
to put in my report?

307
00:35:43,210 --> 00:35:47,640
That some unseen force
made them kill themselves?

308
00:35:47,640 --> 00:35:50,240
We have to go by the evidence.

309
00:35:50,240 --> 00:35:55,015
For now, we'll officially classify the deaths
as suicides.

310
00:35:58,200 --> 00:35:59,509
Look, man...

311
00:36:00,240 --> 00:36:02,610
Some cases can only be closed on paper.

312
00:36:03,600 --> 00:36:06,280
But those who were there that night...

313
00:36:06,280 --> 00:36:08,111
know what really happened.

314
00:36:11,760 --> 00:36:13,305
Let's go with that.

315
00:36:33,400 --> 00:36:35,920
So, according to the autopsy report...

316
00:36:35,920 --> 00:36:39,312
there really was no one else
at the scene, right, Pete?

317
00:36:41,680 --> 00:36:44,472
Forensics confirmed
there were no unidentified fingerprints

318
00:36:44,472 --> 00:36:47,317
or DNA from a fourth person at the scene.

319
00:36:48,520 --> 00:36:51,157
All evidence points
to them attacking one another,

320
00:36:51,157 --> 00:36:53,915
ultimately ending in suicide.

321
00:36:58,200 --> 00:37:00,800
But what happened here
doesn't look like suicide.

322
00:37:03,640 --> 00:37:07,213
It's more like some unseen force
was controlling them.

323
00:37:08,065 --> 00:37:09,213
Exactly.

324
00:37:11,109 --> 00:37:16,904
From a forensic standpoint,
every wound has a distinct injury mechanism.

325
00:37:16,904 --> 00:37:20,061
The force of the knife,
the angle of the stab...

326
00:37:20,061 --> 00:37:22,809
They must be consistent
with human muscle movement.

327
00:37:24,880 --> 00:37:28,312
But their wounds defy the laws of nature.

328
00:37:30,040 --> 00:37:32,712
Science only documents what we can see.

329
00:37:33,760 --> 00:37:37,600
But what we experienced was supernatural.

330
00:37:37,600 --> 00:37:39,600
I don't understand.

331
00:37:39,600 --> 00:37:41,474
They'd already forgiven each other.

332
00:37:41,474 --> 00:37:42,956
And Uncle Chan confirmed

333
00:37:42,956 --> 00:37:46,198
that those spirits
had finally found peace, didn't he?

334
00:37:50,120 --> 00:37:54,808
As a cop, I know that once a complaint is dropped,
the case is closed.

335
00:37:55,840 --> 00:38:00,480
But when it comes to karma,
I'm not so sure anymore.

336
00:38:00,480 --> 00:38:04,583
Can spirits imprisoned for over a hundred years

337
00:38:04,583 --> 00:38:07,804
really end it all
with a single word of forgiveness?

338
00:38:09,886 --> 00:38:11,731
Or perhaps...

339
00:38:11,731 --> 00:38:14,400
they were merely witnesses,

340
00:38:14,400 --> 00:38:18,308
letting the living destroy each other,
driven by their old nature.

341
00:38:21,600 --> 00:38:23,213
So, what are you going to do now?

342
00:38:24,880 --> 00:38:29,615
After Nat's funeral,
I think I'll move somewhere else.

343
00:38:44,920 --> 00:38:48,885
And this will be
the final livestream on this channel.

344
00:38:48,885 --> 00:38:51,120
Because I've started a new channel!

345
00:38:51,120 --> 00:38:53,000
It's called Voices from the Dark.

346
00:38:53,000 --> 00:38:57,025
[I will!]
Don't forget to like and subscribe!

347
00:38:57,025 --> 00:38:58,617
[Will it be even scarier?]
Bye-bye!

348
00:39:06,360 --> 00:39:09,232
I hadn't posted any updates in a long time.

349
00:39:09,232 --> 00:39:12,800
When I checked,
my followers had been asking about it nonstop.

350
00:39:12,800 --> 00:39:16,450
They asked about my early ghost videos
at the great-grandfather's house.

351
00:39:16,450 --> 00:39:20,010
So I decided to do
one final livestream for them.

352
00:39:26,240 --> 00:39:30,909
Speaking of which,
I miss Whan and Aunt Nong too.

353
00:39:32,680 --> 00:39:35,016
They both used to work for me.

354
00:39:36,240 --> 00:39:40,709
And then there's Pam and Nat,
who used to own this house.

355
00:39:42,680 --> 00:39:44,440
It's all in the past now.

356
00:39:44,440 --> 00:39:46,511
Don't dwell on it too much.

357
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:50,009
Didn't you say life must go on?

358
00:39:54,000 --> 00:39:57,632
I may not be able
to erase your painful memories,

359
00:39:57,632 --> 00:39:59,714
but I can be there for you.

360
00:40:00,560 --> 00:40:03,800
As someone who went through all of it with you.

361
00:40:03,800 --> 00:40:05,440
Someone who truly understands

362
00:40:05,440 --> 00:40:07,511
what happened that night.

363
00:40:09,120 --> 00:40:11,506
Thank you for being there for me.

364
00:40:14,200 --> 00:40:20,160
Of course... And I promise
I'll always be by your side.

365
00:40:20,160 --> 00:40:21,714
If you'll let me.

366
00:40:23,240 --> 00:40:25,314
Why wouldn't I?

367
00:40:26,240 --> 00:40:28,420
Friendship is a beautiful thing.

368
00:40:34,840 --> 00:40:36,428
It's time to go.
[Who are those three?]

369
00:40:37,000 --> 00:40:38,280
Let the rest
[Cosplayers?]

370
00:40:38,280 --> 00:40:41,005
be settled by those who take our place.
[Goosebumps!]

371
00:40:50,880 --> 00:40:52,718
Did you hear something?

372
00:40:53,880 --> 00:40:55,410
No, I didn't.

373
00:41:00,320 --> 00:41:02,413
Speaking of Nat...

374
00:41:02,413 --> 00:41:04,518
Shall we go make merit for them?

375
00:41:07,360 --> 00:41:08,801
I'd like that.
